UPDATE companies SET description='DG Medical operates from Centerville, Ohio, and was established in 2010 as a dedicated medical device contract manufacturer. The business grew out of DimcoGray Corporation, a long-standing producer of thermoplastic and thermoset knobs and handles, giving the team more than 30 years of plastics molding experience before the DG Medical name was adopted.

The company provides molding solutions, assembly, prototyping, and packaging services for medical devices. Packaging lines combine automated and manual processes, and engineering support covers mold design and material selection.

DG Medical serves medical device original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), describing its customer base as many of the world''s medical device companies.

The firm emphasizes its FDA registration and ISO 13485 certification, along with full traceability throughout production, as key differentiators. The move to create a separate medical division was described as a natural off‑shoot after years of supplying molded components to the medical industry, leveraging deep knowledge of medical polymers and mold design.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Assembly services", "Prototyping (3-D printed models)", "Packaging (automated and manual)", "Process control monitoring", "Engineering support", "Quality traceability"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Medical device OEMs"], "materials": ["Medical-grade polymers", "Thermoplastics", "Thermosets"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA registered and ISO 13485 certified", "Process control technology for molding monitoring", "Full traceability throughout production", "In-house prototyping with 3-D molded models", "Automated and manual packaging options"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 as DG Medical -> db", "Over 30 years plastics molding experience via DimcoGray Corporation -> db", "FDA Registered and ISO 13485 registered -> db", "Located in Centerville, Ohio -> db", "Services: molding, assembly, prototyping, packaging -> /", "Process control technology for molding -> /", "Traceability throughout production -> /", "Prototyping with 3-D models -> /", "Automated and manual packaging -> /", "Serves medical device OEMs -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "full service contract manufacturer of medical devices", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dg-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DMS Machining & Fabrication was founded in 1991 in Barre, Vermont. The company is led by President/Owner Byron Atwood, who has been with the firm since its inception, alongside Operations Manager & Owner Charlie Atwood and Office Administration Diane Atwood. The business began with a mission to deliver quality work on time and at a fair price, serving industrial, commercial, and construction customers across the Northeast.

The equipment roster includes a range of manual and CNC lathes (Southbend, Southwestern, Poreba, Okuma, Monarch), vertical turret lathes (Bullard), milling machines (Bridgeport, Southwestern CNC, Cincinnati, Futurmill), horizontal boring mills (Wotan, G&L), a Morrison keyseater, and an Eutectic Terodyn thermal‑spray system. The company performs machining, steel and metal fabrication, mechanical repair, design and engineering, and on‑site field services, with rare need for outsourcing.

DMS serves mining, energy (hydropower, biomass), construction, manufacturing, aggregate, asphalt, wood products, educational institutions, hospitals, and ski resorts throughout the Northeast. Its MSHA‑certified field crew travels in fully equipped trucks to handle emergency repairs, planned maintenance, and new installations at customer sites.

The firm emphasizes its enduring commitment to “quality work delivered on time and at a fair price,” backed by continuous investment in skilled personnel, equipment, and stringent safety protocols. This focus has built a reputation for completing complex projects that require both shop‑based precision and on‑site adaptability.', certifications=ARRAY['MSHA Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Machining", "Steel Fabrication", "Metal Fabrication", "Field Services", "Mechanical Repair", "Design & Engineering", "Precision Machine Shop", "Industrial Hydraulic Shop", "On-Site Repair Services", "Inspection & QA", "Thermal Spraying"], "industries": ["Mining", "Energy", "Construction", "Manufacturing", "Hydropower", "Biomass", "Aggregate", "Asphalt", "Wood Products", "Educational", "Hospital", "Ski Resort"], "materials": ["Steel", "Structural steel", "Metal"], "equipment": ["Southbend 12\" Swing 2'' C to C", "Southwestern 18\" Swing 40\" C to C CNC", "Poreba 36\" Swing 17'' C to C", "Meuser 20\" Swing 13'' C to C", "Okuma 22\" Swing 5'' C to C", "Monarch 24\" Swing 4'' C to C", "Monarch 24\" Swing 6'' C to C", "Bullard 36\" Cutmaster", "Bullard 54\" Cutmaster 48\" Under Rail", "Bullard 56\" Cutmaster 72\" Under Rail", "Bullard 76\" Cutmaster 60\" Under Rail", "Hendley 20\" Shaper", "Cincinnati 3'' Radial", "Cincinnati 5'' Radial", "Drill Presses (4)", "Double Spindle (1)", "Morrison Keyseater 8\" x 1\"", "Bridgeport 9\" x 32\" Table 24\" Throat", "Bridgeport 9\" x 42\" Table 24\" Throat", "Bridgeport 9\" x 48\" Table 24\" Throat", "Southwestern CNC x 31\" y 17\" z 23\"", "Cincinnati #4 12\" x 80\" Table 36\" Throat", "Futurmill Opensided Mill 4'' x 4'' x 16'' (w/ Outrigger to allow 10'' Width)", "Cincinnati 9.5\" x 52\" Table 24\" Throat", "Wotan 3\" Spindle 32\" x 39\" Rotary Table", "G & L 4\" Spindle 4'' x 8'' Table", "Wotan 5 \u00bc\" Spindle 4\" x 82\" Rotary Table", "Eutectic Terodyn System 2000", "Bridge cranes (10)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality work delivered on time and at a fair price", "MSHA\u2011certified field crew for on\u2011site work", "45,000+ sq ft facility with 10 bridge cranes", "In\u2011house capabilities minimize outsourcing", "Immediate emergency response capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1991 in Barre, VT -> db, /about-us", "Facility 45,000+ sq ft, 40,000 sq ft main shop, 5,000 sq ft Roadhouse -> /", "Equipment list includes various lathes, mills, boring mills, thermal spray -> /about-us", "Industries served: mining, energy, construction, manufacturing, hydropower, biomass, aggregate, asphalt, wood products, educational, hospital, ski resort -> /", "MSHA Certified field crew -> /", "Leadership: Byron Atwood (President/Owner), Charlie Atwood (Operations Manager & Owner), Diane Atwood (Office Administration) -> /about-us", "Mission: quality work delivered on time and at a fair price -> /about-us", "Services: machining, steel fabrication, field services, mechanical repair, design & engineering, inspection & QA -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DMS Machining is a full service machine shop serving the Northeast since 1991.", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dms-machining-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DS Metal Works, based in Falls Church, Virginia, has been operating since 1945. The company provides custom sheet metal fabrication for residential, commercial, and industrial clients throughout the Washington, D.C. metropolitan area.

The shop produces custom range hoods, kitchen ventilation systems, architectural metalwork, and stainless steel fabrications, along with HVAC ductwork, commercial kitchen equipment, and structural components. Its process moves from consultation and CAD-based design through fabrication to delivery and installation, handling one-off specialty pieces as well as larger commercial projects.

Customers include homeowners, designers, builders, architects, contractors, and business owners in the food-service and commercial sectors. Projects have ranged from a replacement grill grease catcher to full commercial kitchen build-outs and artistic installations such as a large-scale United States map display.

