UPDATE companies SET description='Dakota Metal Solutions LLC operates from a 96,800-square-foot facility in Summit, South Dakota. The company was founded in 2021 with the goal of building a fabrication shop designed for modern manufacturing, combining advanced equipment with efficient production processes.

The shop specializes in high-precision metal fabrication and automated contract manufacturing for OEMs. Its capabilities span fiber laser cutting (sheet up to 5×10 feet, 28 gauge to 1 inch thick), tube laser cutting, CNC milling and turning, automated press brake forming, multi-axis robotic welding, and flat finishing. The facility houses more than 20 advanced machines, including Bystronic 6 kW and 8 kW fiber lasers, a TRUMPF automated press brake, Okuma and Doosan machining centers, and integrated robotic welding cells. An ERP system manages production scheduling and assembly integration, supporting scalable, lights-out production runs.

Dakota Metal Solutions serves OEMs across the Upper Midwest, with delivery throughout North Dakota, South Dakota, Montana, Wyoming, Minnesota, Iowa, and Nebraska. Key industries include agricultural machinery, heavy industrial equipment, construction equipment, truck and trailer manufacturing, and general industrial OEMs. The company produces precision sheet metal components, structural weldments, laser-cut brackets and enclosures, CNC-machined parts, and heavy-equipment sub-assemblies, as well as its own line of steel products such as chip hoppers and hose holders.

The company differentiates itself by engineering the production process—not just the part—through custom fixtures, workholding systems, and in-house automation like the Corsink Pro™ multi-hole drilling system. This approach aims to reduce secondary operations, minimize manual handling, and improve output reliability for repeat production programs.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS Certified Welding Standards','OEM Production Quality Protocols','Automated Repeatability Standards']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-Powered Fiber Laser Cutting (Sheet & Plate up to 1\" Thick)", "Precision Tube Laser Cutting", "Automated Lights-Out Press Brake Forming & Bending", "CNC Milling & Precision Turning", "Integrated Multi-Axis Robotic Welding Cells", "Manual MIG & TIG Welding", "Engineered Production Fixturing & Tooling", "Flat Finishing & Automated Deburring", "Collaborative Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "ERP-Driven Production Scheduling & Assembly Integration"], "industries": ["OEM Equipment Manufacturers", "Agricultural Machinery & Implements", "Heavy Industrial Equipment", "Construction & Infrastructure", "Commercial Metal Fabrication", "Transportation & Material Handling", "Industrial OEM", "Construction Equipment OEM", "Truck & Trailer OEM"], "materials": ["steel", "stainless steel", "aluminum", "copper", "brass", "bronze", "nickel"], "equipment": ["BYSTRONIC 6KW fiber laser", "BYSTRONIC 8KW fiber laser", "BLM TUBE LASER", "220 TON OMEGA press brake", "150 TON BYSTRONIC press brake", "TRUMPF Automated Press Brake", "DOOSAN HP4000 Horizontal Machining Center", "HARDINGE Conquest Turning Center", "OKUMA CNC Milling Machine", "LISMAC SMB XL deburring", "FLADDER finishing", "CLOOS ROBO WELDER", "FANUC WELDER", "DOOSAN + FANUC integrated robotic welding/machining cell"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005\u2033 laser cutting precision; \u00b10.3\u00b0 bend accuracy", "built_on": ["Lights-out capable forming with TRUMPF automated press brake", "I