UPDATE companies SET description='Data-Tel of Louisiana, Inc. was established in Walker, Louisiana, by Emily LeBlanc and Bart LeBlanc. The woman-owned, family-operated business has served the Gulf Coast region for over two decades. The company holds a Louisiana Contractor License (#36386) and is also licensed in Mississippi and Alabama.

Data-Tel designs and installs structured cabling systems, low-voltage wiring, and outside-plant fiber optic and copper infrastructure. With a staff of 12 to 22 employees and an in-house Registered Communications Distribution Designer (RCDD), the firm handles design, project management, installation, and maintenance. It installs roughly 1.4 million feet of cable annually and owns cable testers and fiber fusion splicers for on-demand troubleshooting and emergency repairs.

The company serves commercial retail, government, medical, education, financial, and new-construction/renovation markets. Notable projects include the 8th Air Force War Command Center at Barksdale AFB, Louisiana Heart Hospital, North Oaks renovations, New Orleans Convention Center renovations, Broadmoor Elementary School, and wireless infrastructure deployments for East Baton Rouge, Rapides, and St. Tammany parishes.

Data-Tel differentiates itself by completing most wiring conversions overnight to minimize client downtime, offering 24/7 technician response, and providing manufacturer-backed warranties that can extend beyond 25 years. Its technicians maintain BICSI certifications and participate in ongoing manufacturer training, ensuring installations support speeds up to 40 Gbps.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman-owned','RCDD','BICSI corporate member','BICSI certified installers','Louisiana Contractor License #36386','Mississippi contractor license','Alabama contractor license']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structured cabling design and installation", "Low-voltage systems wiring", "Outside plant fiber optic and copper design and installation", "Cat6/Cat5e voice and data cabling", "Fiber optic cabling", "Multi-pair backbone cabling", "Card access control installation", "Security system cabling", "Fire alarm cable and device installation", "CCTV systems cabling and installation", "Project management", "Maintenance and troubleshooting", "RCDD certified design", "BICSI certified installation"], "industries": ["Commercial retail", "Government", "Medical", "Education", "Financial", "New construction", "Renovations"], "materials": ["Cat6 cable", "Cat5e cable", "Fiber optic cable", "Multi-pair backbone cable", "Copper cable"], "equipment": ["Cable testers", "Fiber fusion splicers"], "volume": "1.4 million feet of cable per year", "lead_time": "Overnight for conversions", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Overnight wiring conversions to minimize downtime", "24/7 technician availability", "In-house cable testers and fiber fusion splicers for rapid troubleshooting", "Manufacturer-backed warranties up to 25 years", "RCDD and BICSI certified staff"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Emily and Bart LeBlanc -> /about", "Woman-owned and family-operated -> /about", "Headquarters in Walker, Louisiana -> /about", "Louisiana Contractor License #36386 -> /", "Licensed in Mississippi and Alabama -> /", "Staff of 12 to 22 employees -> /about, db", "In-house RCDD -> /, /about", "Specializes in structured cabling, low voltage, fiber optic and copper -> /", "Installs 1.4 million feet of cable per year -> /about", "Owns cable testers and fiber fusion splicers -> /about", "24/7 technician availability -> /about, /", "Vertical markets: commercial retail, government, medical, education, financial, new construction/renovations -> /services", "Projects: Barksdale AFB, Louisiana Heart Hospital, North Oaks, New Orleans Convention Center, Broadmoor Elementary, East Baton Rouge Parish, Rapides Parish, St Tammany Parish, LSU Student Recreation Center -> /services", "RCDD certified engineer on staff -> /about", "BICSI corporate member and certified installers -> /about", "Manufacturer warranties up to 25 years -> /about", "Complete conversions in one night -> /about", "Woman-owned certification -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Data-Tel of Louisiana specializes in structured cabling systems, low voltage systems wiring, outside plant fiber optic and copper design and installation.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "12-22", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='data-tel-of-louisiana' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DeVine Woodworking was founded in 2019 by Travis DeVine in Long Island City, New York. The business operates as a family-owned studio; Travis serves as lead artisan and designer while his wife Chelsea DeVine acts as owner and project manager. Travis’s background includes over a decade of apprenticeship with carpenters, electricians, plumbers, and cabinet builders before launching the venture to create sustainably built, durable pieces that blend mid-century modern and art deco influences.

The studio provides a full design-build service for custom furniture and architectural built-ins. Its in-house capabilities cover project management, 3D rendering, furniture design, carpentry, and installation, allowing the team to take a project from concept through final fit-out. Most fabrication occurs in the company’s New York City woodworking shop, which keeps on-site disruption to a minimum; typical installations range from one day for a single piece to two weeks for large built-ins, with a standard living-room unit taking about four to five days.

DeVine Woodworking serves homeowners, apartment renters, and businesses across New York City, as well as architects and interior designers seeking a fabrication partner. Recent projects include a walnut storage cabinet for a Park Slope apartment, a butcher-block kitchen countertop with custom cabinets in Brooklyn, a Murphy bed for an Alphabet City residence, and built-in bookshelves with integrated LED lighting for various Manhattan apartments.

The founders emphasize a collaborative process that starts with a free phone consultation and a $500 deposit covering an in-person measure, a scaled 3D rendering, and one design revision. By handling design, build, and installation internally, the studio aims to deliver pieces that are tailored to each client’s space and lifestyle, built to last generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design-Build", "Project Management", "3D Rendering", "Furniture Design", "Carpentry", "Installation", "Custom Furniture Manufacturing", "Custom Built-In Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Architecture", "Interior Design"], "materials": ["Furniture-grade plywood", "Walnut", "Butcher block", "Painted wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated design-build service: project management, 3D rendering, design, carpentry, and installation under one roof", "Free initial phone consultation with price-range estimate", "Fabrication in NYC studio to minimize on-site installation time", "Installation performed by the company\u2019s own team", "One complimentary design revision included in the initial deposit"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2019 by Travis DeVine -> /about", "Family-owned husband-wife team (Travis and Chelsea DeVine) -> /about", "Headquartered in Long Island City, New York -> db", "Specializes in custom furniture and built-ins -> /", "Offers design-build services including project management, 3D rendering, furniture design, carpentry, installation -> /services", "Serves residential and commercial clients, architects, and designers -> /services", "Projects typically start at $10K, most clients invest $12-30K -> /services", "Fabrication in NYC studio, installation by own team -> /services", "Materials used include furniture-grade plywood, walnut, butcher block -> / (products list)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DeVine Woodworking is a New York City-based design-build woodworking studio specializing in crafting high end custom furniture and built-ins.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='devine-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DeWys Manufacturing began in 1977 when Mark DeWys started the company in a small red barn on his parents’ property in Grand Rapids, Michigan. Drawing on experience from his grandfather’s tool-and-die shop, Mark initially produced tubular fireplace inserts and small metal parts. The business relocated to its current Marne, Michigan facility in 1986, and Mark’s brother Jon DeWys joined in 1987, later assuming leadership after Mark’s passing in 1999. The company remains family-owned.

Today DeWys operates as DeWys Metal Solutions, a full-service contract metal manufacturer offering OEM precision sheet metal fabrication, forming and bending, laser cutting, turret punching, robotic and manual welding, machining, powder coating, product development, assembly, and contract manufacturing. The organization comprises six specialized brands—DeWys Manufacturing, DeWys Stainless Solutions, Wyze Designs, ReFab, Shoreline Powder Coating, and American Grower Resource—serving over 160 customers from a campus at 15300 8th Avenue in Marne. The company highlights its use of a fully automated part-sorting robot for laser cutting, noted as the second such installation in the United States.

The company serves industries including medical equipment, food and beverage, agriculture, renewable energy, data centers, retail fixtures, office furniture, fixed seating, material handling, heavy-duty equipment, electrical equipment, and EV charging. Customers range from OEMs requiring precision components to firms seeking complete contract manufacturing solutions.

DeWys emphasizes its family-owned, American-made identity, lean manufacturing principles, and workforce development through DeWys University, established in 2012. The firm has earned recognition on the Fabricator’s FAB 40 list, multiple Best & Brightest workplace awards, and the MMA Small Tier Manufacturer Award.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["OEM precision sheet metal fabrication", "Sheet metal forming and bending", "Laser cutting", "Turret punching", "Robotic welding", "Manual welding", "Machining", "Powder coating", "Product development", "Product assembly", "Contract manufacturing", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Aluminum fabrication", "Design for manufacturability", "Prototyping", "Kit and finish pack assembly"], "industries": ["Medical Equipment Parts", "Food & Beverage", "Agriculture", "Renewable Energy", "Data Center Solutions", "Retail Fixtures", "Office Furniture", "Fixed Seating", "Material Handling", "Heavy-Duty Equipment", "Electrical Equipment", "EV Charging"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Fully automated part-sorting robot for laser cutting"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, US-based metal fabrication and contract manufacturing", "Full-service capabilities under one roof: fabrication, coating, assembly, and product development", "Advanced automation: fully automated part-sorting robot for laser cutting (second in the nation)", "DeWys University for continuous workforce training since 2012", "Lean manufacturing principles across multiple facilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 by Mark DeWys in Grand Rapids, MI -> db, /, /about", "Family-owned, led by Jon DeWys (CEO) -> /, /about", "Headquarters at 15300 8th Ave, Marne, MI 49435 -> /, /about", "Capabilities: OEM precision sheet metal fabrication, forming & bending, laser cutting, turret punching, welding, machining, powder coating, product development, product assembly, contract manufacturing 