UPDATE companies SET description='Dextronix, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona, with its main office in Portland, Oregon and additional locations in Sacramento and San Diego, California. The company creates affordable implantable medical devices exclusively for veterinary medicine.

Dextronix designs and develops implantable medical devices for veterinary use, including permanent pacemaker systems for dogs, stents and catheters for cats and dogs, and wireless digital diagnostic monitors for cardiology, airway management, and urology. Manufacturing is carried out in France and Germany through partnerships with human medical device manufacturers, such as BS-MTI in France, where core competences include catheter, occluder, balloon, polymer and metal stent fabrication. The company adheres to human medicine quality standards.

Dextronix serves veterinary specialists in cardiology, interventional radiology, surgery, emergency and critical care. Its devices are used by animal clinics and veterinary colleges worldwide for small and large animals, including cats, dogs, horses, and certain exotic animals.

The company was founded to address the lack of affordable implantable medical devices for veterinary use, leveraging human medical device manufacturing standards to provide high-quality, reliable products at lower cost. Dextronix aims to fill the gap where human medical standards are often not available for companion animals.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Interventional device development", "Medical device engineering", "Catheter fabrication", "Occluder fabrication", "Balloon fabrication", "Polymer stent fabrication", "Metal stent fabrication", "Wireless digital diagnostic monitor development", "Pacemaker system development", "Veterinary medical device design"], "industries": ["Veterinary medical devices", "Veterinary equipment", "Animal healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products manufactured in France and Germany to human medical device standards", "Partnerships with leading human medical device manufacturers for design control and cost reduction", "Affordable implantable devices exclusively for veterinary use", "Wireless digital diagnostic monitoring for cardiology, airway management, and urology"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2013 -> db", "Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Main headquarters in Portland, Oregon with locations in Sacramento, San Diego, Phoenix -> /about-us", "Creates affordable implantable medical devices for veterinary medicine -> /", "Initial focus on permanent implantable pacemaker systems for dogs -> /", "Offers stent and catheter products for cats and dogs -> /", "Expanded in 2013 into wireless digital diagnostic monitoring equipment for cardiology, airway management, urology -> /", "Products manufactured in France and Germany to human medical device standards -> /", "Partners with leading human medical device manufacturers (e.g., BS-MTI in France) for production -> /about-us", "Core competences: catheter, occluder, balloon, poly