UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1950 in Danvers, Massachusetts, DiLuigi Foods remains a family-owned operation that has linked tradition with innovation for over seven decades. The company began as a provider of quality meats and has grown into a recognized food manufacturing business serving retail and foodservice channels.

DiLuigi Foods processes beef, chicken, and steak products through SQF-certified facilities. The company maintains an in-house laboratory for rapid raw-material testing and coordinates third-party verification to ensure food safety. A dedicated culinary R&D team develops new products and flavors, conducting extensive taste, texture, color, packaging, and shelf-life testing before market release. Operations span retail and wholesale distribution, with a focus on minimally processed, high-quality meat items.

Its product development cycle explicitly reviews restaurant, retail, and foodservice trends to create items that perform in the marketplace. Customers include both retail buyers seeking branded meat products and foodservice operators requiring consistent quality and innovation.

DiLuigi Foods emphasizes its commitment to food safety and quality as its founding principle. The ownership cites the in-house lab, third-party audits, and SQF certification as key differentiators that allow faster, more accurate quality evaluation. Community involvement, including support for local food banks and national philanthropic efforts, is also noted as part of the company''s mission since 1950.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Certification','USDA Organic']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Meat processing (beef, chicken, steak)", "Product development and R&D (taste, texture, color, packaging, shelf-life testing)", "In-house laboratory testing", "Third-party testing coordination", "Retail and wholesale distribution", "SQF certified manufacturing"], "industries": ["Retail", "Foodservice", "Restaurant"], "materials": ["Beef", "Chicken", "Steak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SQF certification recognized by GFSI", "In-house laboratory for rapid raw-material and production testing", "Third-party verification of quality and safety processes", "Culinary R&D team developing products from market trend analysis", "Family-owned continuity since 1950"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Danvers, Massachusetts -> db", "SQF certified -> /about-us, /quality", "USDA Organic certification -> db", "In-house laboratory -> /about-us", "Third-party testing -> /about-us", "Culinary R&D team and product development process -> /about-us", "Serves retail and foodservice customers -> /about-us", "Reviews restaurant, retail, foodservice trends -> /about-us", "Community support (food banks, police, breast cancer research) -> /about-us", "Minimally processed, high-quality meats -> /quality", "GFSI recognition of SQF -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "DiLuigi Foods is one of the most trusted food manufacturing companies", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='diluigi-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Dickson Furniture Manufacturers was founded by Jim Dickson in 1976 in Houston, Texas. The privately owned company began with a principle of creating exceptional value through uncompromising quality, and has since grown into a vertically integrated contract furniture manufacturer serving commercial markets nationwide.

Operating from a 500,000-square-foot facility in Houston, Dickson produces casegoods, upholstered seating, and structured seating in-house. The plant runs automated TFL and HPL lines, CNC beam saws, routers, edge banders, and dedicated upholstery equipment including CNC fabric and foam cutters. Monthly output exceeds 50,000 casegoods and 5,000 upholstered pieces, with additional capacity for mattress production and powder-coated metal frames. The company also handles delivery and installation.

Dickson serves the hospitality, student housing, multi-unit housing, government, and military sectors. It is a preferred or approved vendor for more than a dozen national hotel brands and has furnished over 10,000 properties across the United States and its territories, including select-service and upper select-service hotels, student communities, and public-sector housing.

The company emphasizes its domestic supply chain, sourcing most materials from suppliers within two hours of the Houston plant to ensure consistent quality, predictable lead times, and reduced transportation impact. Dickson’s in-house laminate layup provides greater finish flexibility, while its vertically integrated model allows full control over quality, timelines, and innovation. The firm describes itself as built to last, not to sell, with continual reinvestment in manufacturing technology such as a recent $10 million TFL line.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Casegoods Manufacturing", "Upholstery Manufacturing", "Structured Seating Manufacturing", "CNC Fabric Cutting", "CNC Foam Cutting", "Powder-Coated Metal Frames", "Mattress Production", "Delivery and Installation", "Automated TFL Line", "HPL Line", "CNC Beam Saw", "CNC Routers", "CNC Edge Banders", "Contour Edge Banders", "Automated Machining Centers", "Doweling Machines", "Dovetailers", "Box Making Equipment", "Fiber/Down Blow Machine", "Bagging Machines", "Industrial Sewing Machines", "Sleeper Sofa Manufacturing", "Leggett & Platt Sleeper Mechanisms", "High-Pressure Laminate (HPL) Tops"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Student Housing", "Multi-Unit Housing", "Government", "Military"], "materials": ["High-pressure laminate (HPL)", "Thermally fused laminate (TFL)", "Angel hair fill", "Leggett & Platt sleeper mechanisms", "Powder-coated metal", "Fabric", "Foam"], "equipment": ["Automated TFL Line", "HPL Line", "Angular CNC Beam Saw", "CNC Beam Saw", "Automated CNC Chop Saw", "Automated CNC Routers", "High-Performance CNC Edge Banders", "Contour Edge Banders", "Automated Machining Centers", "Doweling Machines", "Dovetailers", "Box Making Equipment", "CNC Foam Cutter", "CNC Fabric Cutter", "Fiber/Down Blow Machine", "Bagging Machines", "Industrial Sewing Machines", "Leggett & Platt sleeper mechanisms"], "volume": "50,000+ casegoods per month; 5,000+ upholstered pieces per month", "