UPDATE companies SET description='Dimatic Die & Tool Co. was founded in 1961 in South Omaha, Nebraska, by toolmakers Robert Drvol and Guenter Sobeck. The two-person shop started on 13th Street across from Sokol Auditorium with two machines. In 1978 the company moved to its current 67,000-square-foot facility at 9520 North 48th Street in Omaha.

The shop produces turned parts from 1/4 to 8 inches in diameter, milled parts up to 20 by 20 inches, and runs volumes from one to 100,000 pieces. It also manufactures pressed and solid steel pulleys ranging from 2.5 to 16 inches.

Dimatic serves a mix of Fortune 500 corporations, mid-size manufacturers, distributors, and small businesses across the United States and internationally. Typical components include enclosures, cases, housings, brackets, bearing retainers, electrical parts, and pulleys for industrial and commercial equipment.

The company emphasizes single-source responsibility—design, tooling, production, warehousing, and distribution under one roof—and cites its ISO-based quality system, an average toolmaker tenure of more than 25 years, and a central U.S. location near I-680 and Eppley Airfield as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tool and die design and build (molds, dies, fixtures, tools)", "3D part and tool design (ProEngineer, SolidWorks)", "Mold design and construction (hot/insulated runner, stack, unscrewing, insert, cam/hydraulic core pull)", "Die design and construction (compound, progressive, blank/pierce/cutoff)", "Injection molding (55\u2013880 ton machines)", "Production stamping (up to 165 ton presses)", "CNC machining (machining centers, turning centers, lathes)", "CNC EDM and wire EDM", "Conventional milling, boring, grinding", "Pressed and solid steel pulleys (2.5\u2033\u201316\u2033)", "Assembly of machined parts", "Automated production painting", "Special packaging and kitting", "Warehousing and inventory management", "3D printed prototype models", "In-house mold finishing (texturing, polishing, lettering, logo imprinting)", "CAD/CAM integration"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Steel", "Plastics", "Aluminum", "Brass"], "equipment": ["CNC machining centers", "CNC turning centers", "CNC lathes", "CNC EDM", "Wire EDM", "Conventional mills", "Boring machines", "Grinders", "Injection molding machines (55\u2013880 ton)", "Stamping presses (up to 165 ton)", "Automated painting line", "3D printers (prototyping)", "CAD/CAM software: ProEngineer, SolidWorks"], "volume": "1 to 100,000 parts", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source responsibility: design, tooling, manufacturing, and distribution under one roof", "ISO-based manufacturing and quality systems", "Warehousing and stocking of critical customer parts", "Central U.S. location with direct interstate and airport access", "Average toolmaker experien