UPDATE companies SET description='Eco-Panels of Tennessee, Inc. operates from Red Boiling Springs in Clay County, Tennessee, with its 35,000-square-foot manufacturing plant in nearby Hermitage Springs. The company was established in 2012 as a licensed franchise location for Eco-Panels, LLC of Mocksville, North Carolina, expanding to meet rising demand for structural insulated panels. It belongs to a family-owned group of businesses that has produced systems-built housing products and forestry commodities since the late 1970s, making it the largest non-governmental employer in the area.

The facility manufactures high-performance structural insulated panels (SIPs) for residential and commercial building applications. Using state-of-the-art technology, the plant produces panels in a wide variety of sizes, shapes, and configurations, achieving insulation values of R-26 in 4.5-inch panels and R-40 in 6.5-inch panels. The panels are described as two to three times stronger than conventional framing, with a foam core that contains no volatile organic compounds and does not melt at any temperature.

Eco-Panels serves homeowners, builders, and architects across the residential and commercial construction sectors, including timber-frame projects. Testimonials cite successful collaborations with individual homeowners such as Micah Mazanowski and Eric O’Donnell, as well as firms like 423 Dwell, LLC and licensed contractor Roger West. The company provides design assistance, installation guidance, and on-site training to support both professional crews and DIY builders.

The business was founded to offer a more economical, sustainable, and safer alternative to traditional construction. The company emphasizes lower utility, building, and labor costs with less waste, long-term energy savings, and reduced wood usage. As a franchise of the North Carolina–based Eco-Panels system, it leverages a proprietary panel technology marketed for its strength, environmental profile, and speed of assembly.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural insulated panel manufacturing", "SIP panel design and engineering", "Precision panel fabrication (cutting, shaping)", "Custom panel sizes, shapes, and configurations", "Residential building envelope systems", "Commercial building envelope systems", "Timber-frame integration packages", "Installation guidance and on-site training", "Builder and architect technical support", "Homeowner DIY project support", "Panel delivery and logistics coordination", "Plant tours and customer visits", "Energy-efficient building solutions", "Sustainable building material production", "Low-waste manufacturing processes"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Timber frame construction", "Architectural design services", "Builder/contractor services", "Homeowner/DIY market"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry-leading R-26 in 4.5\u2033 panels and R-40 in 6.5\u2033 panels", "Panels rated 2\u20133\u00d7 stronger than conventional framing", "Foam core with no VOCs and no melt temperature", "Licensed franchise of the Eco-Panels system from Mocksville, NC", "Family-owned group operating in Clay County since the late 1970s"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 -> db", "Headquarters Red Boiling Springs, Tennessee -> db", "Family-owned group of businesses -> /about-us", "Licensed franchise of Eco-Panels, LLC (Mocksville, NC) -> /about-us", "Manufacturing plant 35,000 sq ft in Hermitage Springs, Tennessee -> /a