UPDATE companies SET description='Elsmere Ironworks has operated from Elsmere, Kentucky, since 1958. The family-owned shop was purchased in 2023 by Ryan Work from longtime owners John and Dan Goderwis, continuing a legacy of custom ornamental ironwork for the Tri-State region.

The company fabricates exterior and interior railings, estate gates, fencing, balconies, window boxes, wine gates, and security features for windows and doors. Its workshop combines old-world forging techniques with modern welding, powder coating, custom faux finishes, and hot-dipped galvanizing. A showroom allows clients to review samples and collaborate with CAD designers on custom projects.

Elsmere Ironworks serves residential and commercial customers across Greater Cincinnati, Northern Kentucky, and Southern Indiana. Homeowners request railings, gates, and decorative accents, while commercial projects include security installations and architectural metalwork.

The firm emphasizes durable finishes — powder coating baked in an oven for ten times the durability of paint, and hot-dipped galvanizing rated for 70-plus years of corrosion resistance — backed by a one-year paint warranty. It also stresses on-time delivery and free estimates.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom iron fabrication", "Welding (old-world and modern)", "Exterior railing fabrication", "Interior railing fabrication", "Estate gate fabrication", "Fencing fabrication", "Balcony and mock balcony fabrication", "Window box fabrication", "Wine gate fabrication", "Security fabrication for windows and doors", "Powder coating", "Custom faux finishing", "Hot-dipped galvanizing", "CAD design collaboration", "Free estimates", "Installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Wrought iron", "Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8-12 weeks for fabrication", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1958", "Old-world forging techniques combined with modern welding and coating technology", "Powder coating baked in oven for ten times the durability of standard paint", "Hot-dipped galvanizing providing 70+ years of corrosion resistance", "One-year paint warranty on finished products"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 -> db, /about", "Location Elsmere, KY -> db, /", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Ryan Work purchased in 2023 from John and Dan Goderwis -> /about", "Services: railings, gates, fencing, balconies, window boxes, wine gates, security -> /, /services", "Processes: welding, powder coating, custom faux finish, hot-dipped galvanizing -> /services", "Lead time 8-12 weeks for fabrication -> /services", "One-year paint warranty -> /services", "Materials: wrought iron and steel -> /about", "Serves residential and commercial in Tri-State area -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Elsmere Ironworks from its inception has had one goal: to fabricate high quality, functional and long-lasting metal works that exceed customer expectations.", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/elsmere-ironworks/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elsmere-ironworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='EnTech Plastics, Inc. operates from a 45,000-square-foot facility in Corry, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1996, the company has built its reputation on solving difficult molding challenges that other suppliers cannot.

The shop specializes in low- to mid-volume custom injection molding on machines ranging from 44 to 1,100 tons, producing parts from 1 gram up to 22 pounds. Core processes include gas-assist, insert molding, over molding, and master unit die (MUD) frames, supported by closed-loop controllers, SPC monitoring, and real-time production tracking. The facility dedicates 25,000 square feet to manufacturing and 20,000 square feet to warehousing with nine loading docks. Engineering services cover design for manufacturability, tool building, resin selection (including high-temperature grades such as PEI, PPS, and PEEK), and full assembly.

Customers span heavy-duty truck, medical, industrial, and consumer markets. EnTech has produced large components such as truck body panels, medical device housings, industrial machinery covers, and consumer product parts. Long-term clients include ANDRITZ Pulp & Paper and other OEMs that moved work to EnTech after experiencing inconsistent quality from larger molders.

The company positions itself on the intersection of low volume and high tonnage—a combination that is rare in the industry—and on delivering parts that are both aesthetically precise and mechanically robust. Its stated differentiator is the willingness to take on problematic tooling or nonconforming parts, diagnose root causes, and re-engineer the process to achieve consistent output.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Injection Molding", "Gas Assist Injection Molding", "Insert Molding", "Over Molding", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Tool Building and Design Assistance", "Engineered Resin Selection", "Assembly and Value-Added Services", "Low Volume / High Tonnage Molding", "Master Unit Die (MUD) Frames", "New Product Introductions", "Tool Transfers", "Reshoring of Plastic Parts", "Metal-to-Plastic Conversion", "Resin Evaluation and Substitution", "SPC Process Monitoring", "Real-Time Production Monitoring", "Closed-Loop Process Control", "Core Pull and Air Eject", "Automatic Material Loading", "Customized Inspection Equipment"], "industries": ["Heavy-Duty Truck", "Medical", "Industrial", "Consumer"], "materials": ["Engineering resins", "General-purpose resins", "High-temperature resins (PEI, PPS, PEEK)"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines 44\u20131,100 tons", "Core pull and air eject systems", "Ceramic heater bands", "Hardened screws and barrels", "Automatic material loading systems", "Customized inspection equipment", "Cooling towers and chillers with filters and water treatment", "Thermolators (water and oil)", "Desiccant and hot air dryers", "Mold temperature controllers", "Air compressors with drying systems", "Overhead cranes", "Quality monitoring system", "Integrated plant-wide ERP system", "Fire protection system"], "volume": "Low to mid volume; low volume programs under 1,000 parts/year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low-volume production on high-tonnage presses (up to 1,100 tons)", "Gas-assist injection molding for complex geometries", "Insert and over molding capabilities", "Real-time production monitoring with SPC and closed-loop control", "In-house tool design and build with guaranteed part quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Corry, Pennsylvania -> db", "45,000 sq ft facility, 25k manufacturing, 20k warehouse, 9 loading docks -> /about", "Machines 44\u20131,100 tons -> /about", "Part weight 1 gram to 22 pounds -> /about", "Gas assist, insert molding, over molding, MUD frames -> /services", "Closed-loop controllers, SPC, real-time monitoring -> /about", "Industries: heavy-duty truck, medical, industrial, consumer -> /about", "Client ANDRITZ Pulp & Paper -> /about", "Engineering services: DFM, tool building, resin selection, assembly -> /about and /services", "High-temp resins PEI, PPS, PEEK mentioned in blog -> /services", "Low volume runs under 1,000 parts/year -> /services", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a full-service custom injection molding company", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/entech-plastics-inc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='entech-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Encore Wire Corporation operates a 3.5 million-square-foot campus in McKinney, Texas. The company was founded in 1989 and manufactures building wire and copper cable for residential, commercial, and industrial construction markets.

The company engineers, manufactures, and ships UL-rated copper electrical wire from its Texas facility, which houses a dedicated quality control lab known as the Encore Wire TechLab®. Its product line includes building wire and copper cable, supplemented by proprietary packaging systems such as the Reel Payoff®, Cyclone Barrel Pack®, PullPro®, MC Barrel Pack, Reel Deal®, and Reel Payoff® Premium. The campus employs over 1,000 people and supports production for sustainable energy applications including solar, electric vehicle charging, battery storage, wind, and utility transmission.

Encore Wire serves residential, commercial, and industrial construction sectors, as well as renewable energy markets. Its products are used in hospitals, where reliable power is critical, and in everyday infrastructure such as lighting for sports venues and residential charging. The company emphasizes American-made manufacturing and rapid delivery to meet project timelines.

Encore Wire differentiates itself through vertical integration and self-reliance, controlling engineering, manufacturing, and shipping on a single campus. The company highlights its ''whatever it takes'' customer service, delivery times, and innovative packaging designed to reduce labor and scrap on job sites. Its TechLab® ensures products meet stringent quality standards before shipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire manufacturing", "Cable manufacturing", "Quality control (TechLab\u00ae)", "Custom packaging solutions", "Sustainable energy wire and cable solutions", "UL-rated copper electrical wire production", "Building wire production", "Copper cable production"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Industrial construction", "Solar energy", "Electric vehicles", "Battery storage", "Wind energy", "Utility transmission", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Copper"], "equipment": ["Encore Wire TechLab\u00ae", "Reel Payoff\u00ae", "Cyclone Barrel Pack\u00ae", "PullPro\u00ae", "MC Barrel Pack", "Reel Deal\u00ae", "Reel Payoff\u00ae Premium"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["3.5 million-square-foot integrated campus in McKinney, Texas", "American-made wire and cable with industry-leading delivery times", "Encore Wire TechLab\u00ae for in-house quality control", "Proprietary packaging systems (Reel Payoff\u00ae, Cyclone Barrel Pack\u00ae, PullPro\u00ae) that reduce installation labor", "Full product line for sustainable energy projects including solar, EV, battery storage, wind, and utility transmission"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 -> db", "Headquarters in McKinney, Texas -> db", "3.5 million-square-foot campus -> page /", "1000+ employees -> db", "Manufactures building wire and copper cable -> db, page /", "UL-rated copper electrical wire -> db", "Serves residential, commercial, industrial construction -> db", "Sustainable solutions for solar, EV, battery storage, wind,