UPDATE companies SET description='Enphase Energy was founded in 2006 by Raghu Belur and Martin Fornage in California. The company is now headquartered in Milpitas, California, and operates as a publicly traded corporation (NASDAQ: ENPH).

The company designs and manufactures solar microinverters, battery energy storage systems, and energy management software. Its global workforce numbers about 2,686 employees, and production is carried out at contract manufacturing facilities in South Carolina and Texas.

Enphase serves residential, commercial, and utility-scale solar markets. Its products are installed by a network of over 5,000 installers worldwide and are used by homeowners, businesses, and utility operators seeking distributed energy solutions. The company also provides design, permitting, and monitoring platforms—such as System Planner, Solargraf, and the Enphase App—to support installers and system owners.

Enphase says its microinverter architecture converts sunlight into a safe, reliable, and scalable energy source, with intelligent microinverters compatible with virtually any solar panel. Paired with award-winning battery technology and an monitoring app, the system aims to give users unprecedented data and control over their energy production and consumption, advancing what the company calls a sustainable future for all.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Microinverter design and manufacturing", "Battery energy storage system design", "Energy management software development", "Solar system design and planning (System Planner)", "Permitting and proposal platform (Solargraf)", "Installer training and certification (Enphase University)", "System monitoring and diagnostics", "System ownership transfer services"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Utility"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Microinverter technology compatible with virtually any solar panel", "Award-winning smart battery storage systems", "Industry-leading monitoring app with panel-level data", "U.S. contract manufacturing in South Carolina and Texas", "Installer-focused platforms for design, permitting, and training"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 by Raghu Belur and Martin Fornage in California -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Milpitas, California -> db", "2,686 employees and personnel across global offices -> /about-us", "Approximately 89.4 million microinverters shipped since inception -> /about-us", "Approximately 5.3 million Enphase-based systems deployed in over 165 countries -> /about-us", "Manufacturing at contract facilities in the United States (South Carolina and Texas) -> /about-us, /", "Products: solar microinverters, energy storage systems, energy management software -> db, /, /about-us", "Industries served: Residential, Commercial, Utility -> db", "5,000+ installers worldwide -> /about-