-d-menold-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Evans Manufacturing Co. operates from Marysville, Washington, tracing its roots to 1916 when it began as a wire-forming operation. The business changed hands several times before Rod and Mary Long acquired it in 2003, bringing Rod’s production manufacturing experience. In its early years the company ran out of a garage; today it occupies a modern facility equipped with CNC laser cutters, press brakes, and wire-forming machinery.

The shop provides a range of metal fabrication services: laser cutting of sheet metal using a Cincinnati system with an nLight source, CNC bending on press brakes, wire bending on Wafios equipment, MIG/TIG/spot welding of steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, hardware insertion via a Haegar machine, and laser engraving for part marking with an Epilog laser. It produces wire forms such as springs and clips, sheet metal components, and proprietary lines including household items, pet supplies, tech accessories, office supplies, and orchard products.

Customers span agriculture, food production, marine, dairy, medical, and pharmaceutical sectors, as well as military, defense, aerospace, and avionics programs. The company’s wire-forming heritage also serves the commercial fishing industry.

Evans emphasizes treating customer priorities as its own, citing on-time delivery, quality focus, and straightforward communication as differentiators. The ownership team highlights the pain of inflexible suppliers and positions the company as a responsive, quality-driven partner.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Sheet metal bending", "Wire bending", "Welding (MIG, TIG, spot)", "Metal finishing & coating", "Hardware insertion", "Parts marking / laser engraving"], "industries": ["Agricultural", "Food Production", "Marine", "Dairy", "Medical", "Pharmaceutical", "Military and defense", "Aerospace and avionics", "Commercial fishing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Cincinnati laser cutter with nLight light source", "Wafios machines", "Haegar hardware machine", "Epilog laser"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Cincinnati laser cutter with nLight light source", "Wafios CNC wire forming machines", "Haegar hardware insertion machine", "Epilog laser for part marking", "Family-owned operation since 2003"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1916 -> db", "Headquarters Marysville, Washington -> db", "Family-owned, bought by Rod and Mary Long in 2003 -> /about-us", "Started in garage, now modern facility -> /about-us", "Capabilities: laser cutting, bending, wire bending, welding, metal finishing & coating, hardware insertion, parts marking -> /", "Equipment: Cincinnati laser cutter with nLight light source, Wafios machines, Haegar hardware machine, Epilog laser -> /", "Industries: Agricultural, Food Production, Marine, Dairy, Medical, Pharmaceutical, Military and defense, Aerospace and avionics -> /", "Materials: steel, stainless, aluminum -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /", "Ownership: Family-owned -> /about-us", "Proprietary products: household items, pet supplies, tech, office supplies, orchard products -> /", "Wire forming heritage for commercial fishing -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture a number of different products including household items, pet supplies, tech, and office supplies.", "founded_year": "1916", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='evans-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Excal Inc. operates a brass and bronze sand casting foundry in Mills, Wyoming, from an 85,000-square-foot facility that opened in 1991 when founder Fred Harmon relocated the business from its predecessor, Buckeye Brass Foundry (established 1966). The company employs more than 50 people and is now a member of the Foundrion Group, a network of non‑ferrous foundries across North America.

The foundry produces sand castings weighing 1 to 2,000 pounds in a wide range of brass, bronze, and stainless‑steel alloys. Two independent high‑production green‑sand molding lines and two no‑bake/air‑set lines run alongside four melting furnaces capable of 60,000 pounds per day. In‑house capabilities include pattern making, coremaking (with a custom Palmer Coremaker), heat treating, five CNC turning centers, two CNC mills, spectrometer inspection, and an ERP system for full traceability.

Excal serves industries such as pump and valve, water metering, fire protection, electrical, lighting, marine, irrigation, water treatment, and broader waterworks, infrastructure, and energy markets. Customers range from prototype programs to multi‑thousand‑part production runs, all machined to finished condition under one roof.

