UPDATE companies SET description='FPEC Corp. was founded in 1959 by John H. Davison and Armond Villian in a small shed behind a lumberyard in Bellflower, California. The company, now headquartered in Springdale, Arkansas, remains family-owned and operated, currently in its third and fourth generations. The founders started the business after recognizing that food processors were left waiting for late equipment, stuck with underperforming machines, and struggling to get responsive service.

FPEC designs and manufactures food processing equipment and material handling systems for the meat, poultry, pork, beef, and pet food industries. Their product line includes grinders, tumblers, cookers, mixers, conveyors, lifts, dumpers, and automation solutions with custom control panels. The company emphasizes 100% stainless steel construction with precision welding for unibody strength.

The company serves food processors nationwide, including poultry, pork, and beef operations as well as pet food manufacturers. Customers range from large poultry producers to smaller processors seeking integrated production lines from intake to packaging. Testimonials reference maintenance managers and plant personnel who value reduced downtime and easier maintenance.

FPEC differentiates itself by building its own controls for all equipment, enabling smoother startups, and by maintaining a long-term partnership model that includes responsive parts shipping and service. The founders'' original vision—to challenge the status quo of late deliveries and poor service—continues to drive the company''s engineering-first approach and commitment to American-made quality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food processing equipment design and manufacturing", "Material handling systems design and manufacturing", "Automation and control systems integration", "Custom control panel fabrication", "Equipment installation and startup support", "Replacement parts supply", "On-site service and maintenance", "Production line layout design", "Sanitary stainless steel welding", "Equipment retrofits and upgrades"], "industries": ["Meat processing", "Poultry processing", "Pork processing", "Beef processing", "Pet food processing", "Food processing"], "materials": ["Stainless steel (100%)", "Precision welded stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Chain Dumper Lift", "Hylift Dumper", "Pivot Dumper", "Lab Mixer", "Mixer Grinder", "Sheet Meat Horn", "Meat grinders", "Tumblers", "Cookers", "Conveyors", "Lifts", "Dumpers", "Control panels"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% stainless steel, precision welded (not bolted) for unibody construction", "In-house control panel design and fabrication for all equipment", "Overnight shipping on replacement parts", "On-site service technicians available", "Family-owned continuity since 1959"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1959 by John H. Davison and Armond Villian -> /about", "Family-owned, third/fourth generation -> /about", "Headquartered in Springdale, Arkansas (db) / Fayetteville, Arkansas (website) -> db, /", "Designs and manufactures food processing equipment (grinders, tumblers, cookers, mixers) -> /", "Material handling systems (conveyors, lifts, dumpers) -> /"